          runoffs where every seat sees the tally <b>and the dissenters’ arguments</b>. Honest caveats:
          hiding names makes self-selection harder, not impossible, and on a two-CLI roster 75% means
          unanimity — when nothing differentiates, plurality stands and the recorded dissent is the value.
